  "worked_solution": "The complement of $Y,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{Y},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $Y.$ To represent $\\overset{\u2015}{Y},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $Y,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/25b1388466c800664b7d438eabf58cafd365174ca877abff8cd0465e2b23e7cb.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $10,$ and $101.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $Y.$ Therefore, the complement of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{Y}={10,101}.\n$$",
